A small software update that fixes bugs (functionality issues), security issues, or adds new features.

How it is Used

The County may send out patches as quick fixes to public-facing tools and services, like the County’s Public Permit Portal. Patches are often temporary solutions meant to keep things running smoothly until a more complete update can be made later.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:1:{s:12:"glossary:bug";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1744831260;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744831260;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:14:"glossary:patch";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:504;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}}}